Fix memDecompress(type = "gzip") looping forever on a truncated gzip
or zlib stream, on builds without libdeflate.

R_uncompress() in gzio.h writes stream.total_out through its destLen
argument on every return, not only on success.  do_memDecompress()
passes outlen by reference and treats Z_BUF_ERROR as "the output
buffer was too small", doubling outlen and retrying.  That is right
when the buffer really filled up (total_out == buffer size), but
inflate() also returns Z_BUF_ERROR when the input runs out before the
end of the stream.  Then total_out is just the number of bytes decoded
so far, independent of the buffer size, so the "doubled" size is the
same on every pass and the loop never terminates.  Each pass
R_alloc()s another buffer that stays live until the call returns:

    ==254== ERROR: libFuzzer: out-of-memory (used: 2829Mb; limit: 2560Mb)
    3722675704 byte(s) (98%) in 91984 allocation(s)
        #1 Rf_allocVector3   src/main/memory.c:2895
        #3 R_alloc           src/main/memory.c:2333
        #4 do_memDecompress  src/main/connections.c:7303

A stream that produced nothing at all (a zlib header plus two bytes)
spins at zero bytes instead and shows up as a timeout.

Track the size of the buffer just allocated separately, grow only when
Z_BUF_ERROR comes back with that buffer completely filled, and
otherwise fall through to the existing "internal error" report.  The
libdeflate branch is a separate loop keyed on
LIBDEFLATE_INSUFFICIENT_SPACE and is not affected; the OSS-Fuzz image
has no libdeflate, so it takes the zlib path.

Found by fuzzing R with libFuzzer + AddressSanitizer (OSS-Fuzz
decompress target, testcases 5726025607348224 and 6383420146778112
(out-of-memory) and 6066205270802432 (timeout)).

Upstream status: reported as R Bugzilla bug 19200 with this fix
attached (attachment 3894; also r-devel/r-svn PR #357).  The upstream
patch also adds a regression test to tests/reg-tests-1e.R, left out
here so this carry patch does not go stale with that file.  Delete this
patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report it as
already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

diff --git a/src/main/connections.c b/src/main/connections.c
index a4905eeecb..aa93a55337 100644
--- a/src/main/connections.c
+++ b/src/main/connections.c
@@ -7340,15 +7340,20 @@ do_memDecompress(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 	    opt = 16;  // force gzip format
 	}
 	while(1) {
-	    buf = (Bytef *) R_alloc(outlen, sizeof(Bytef));
-	    // R_uncompress is in gzio.h
+	    uLong buflen = outlen;
+	    buf = (Bytef *) R_alloc(buflen, sizeof(Bytef));
+	    // R_uncompress is in gzio.h.  It sets outlen to the number of
+	    // bytes actually produced, whatever the result.
 	    int res = R_uncompress(buf, &outlen, p, inlen, opt);
-	    if(res == Z_BUF_ERROR) {
-		if(outlen < ULONG_MAX/2) {
-		    outlen *= 2; continue;
+	    if(res == Z_BUF_ERROR && outlen == buflen) {
+		// the output buffer filled up: grow it and retry
+		if(buflen < ULONG_MAX/2) {
+		    outlen = buflen ? 2*buflen : 1; continue;
 		} else break;
 	    }
 	    if(res >= 0) break;
+	    // Z_BUF_ERROR with room left in the buffer means the input
+	    // ended prematurely, so a bigger buffer cannot help.
 	    error("internal error %d in memDecompress(%s)", res,
 		  "type = \"gzip\"");
 	}
